'''Summon Elemental Relic''' is an [[trigger]]ed [[minion]] [[skill]] granted by [[Unwavering Crusade]], a Notable [[Ascendancy]] passive skill for the [[Guardian]]. It has a chance to trigger when you or your [[ally|allies]] kill an enemy or hit a rare or unique enemy.

The skill summons an Elemental Relic of [[fire]], [[cold]], or [[lightning]], chosen at random. Each Elemental Relic has a special version of an {{il|Anger}}, {{il|Hatred}}, or {{il|Wrath}} aura respectively, and [[explode]] dealing damage of their respective element on [[death]] (or duration expiry) in an area around them. If the skill chooses an element of a Relic that is already summoned, the duration is refreshed instead.

==Mechanics==
Summon Elemental Relic has a [[cooldown]] of 0.3 seconds which can be scaled with [[cooldown recovery]].

Elemental Relics are capped at one of each element. They have a base duration of 5 seconds. They have a defensive AI, following close to the character, and are unable to use any damaging skills. Their explosion on death deals 100% of their maximum life as their respective element.

'''Auras''': The auras used by Elemental Relics scale based on the minion's level, which in turn scales off of the player's [[character]] level, up to 85. At the maximum level of 85, the auras grant the following stats<ref>https://www.pathofexile.com/forum/view-thread/3408278</ref>:
: {{il|Anger}} grants 182 to 259 added fire damage to attacks and spells.
: {{il|Hatred}} grants 43% of physical damage as extra cold damage.
: {{il|Wrath}} granted 26 to 415 added lightning damage to attacks and 23% more spell lightning damage
These values are equivalent to a Level 27.5 Anger, Level 27 Hatred, and Level 27.25 Wrath. The values granted by the auras may not necessarily match those of their respective gems due to gems only showing values at fixed level intervals.

One reliable way to explode Elemental Relic is by using {{il|Tukohama's Fortress}} as it will provide [[Blood Magic]] to your minions, with allocated [[Necromantic Aegis]]. As Elemental Relic will always cast their respective auras after being summoned which costs 50% of mana, is now converted to cost 50% of their life instead, putting them on low life and being able to detonate thanks to [[Minion Instability]].
This way relic will effectively deal 100% of their maximum life as their respective element + 33% of their maximum life as fire damage.

Internally, Summon Elemental Relic has the <code>RandomElement</code> skill tag, causing it to function as if it was a [[Prismatic]] skill. This causes it to be modified by [[Combat Focus]] to prevent certain elements from being chosen when spawning a random element Elemental Relic. However, this does not bypass the maximum number of each element Elemental Relic allowed. For example, using both {{il|page=Combat Focus (Crimson Jewel)}} and {{il|page=Combat Focus (Cobalt Jewel)}} prevents Cold and Fire Elemental Relics, so it will always summon a Lightning Elemental Relic, but will still be limited at a maximum of 1 Lightning Elemental Relic.

